  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nContinued north to northwest flow will continue to pull in\nenough moisture to result in scattered rain and snow showers.\nThese showers will be aided by the passage of several mid-level\ndisturbances. Opted to keep the temperatures a little warmer at\nnight and cooler during the day due to the clouds and\nprecipitation. More winter like temperature values in the 30's\nand 40's should continue. Model soundings do show the potential\nfor a few afternoon wind gusts close to 20 mph Saturday with\nslightly lower values Sunday. Any snow showers may result in\nminor snow accumulations. The expected wind direction favors\nwestern Madison county to Tully and perhaps Ithaca areas. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA ridge of high pressure will build into the region early next week. \nLake clouds will prevent little sunshine from peeking through on \nMonday but sunny skies return on Tuesday. Daytime temperatures will \ntrend warmer throughout the week with the potential for some 60s on \nThursday and Friday. Nightly temperatures will stay cool, often \nfalling below freezing. Despite this, most of next week will be dry \nwith surface high pressure in control.",
